# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .dockerignore — prevents large/unneeded files from reaching the build context
#
# NOTE: server/dist/ and server/package.json are NOT excluded — the backend
# Dockerfile (Dockerfile.backend) needs them to build the API image.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.vercel/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
trace.txt
tail.txt
rows.txt
build*.txt
check-features.cjs
validate-yaml.cjs
.env
.env.local
.env.docker
*.env*
# Runtime credentials — MUST never be baked into the image. Bare `db-config.json`
# only matches the context root, NOT the nested `server/dist/` copy that
# Dockerfile.backend COPYs. Use `**/` so the dev machine's setup PIN + DB password
# can't leak into the image and get initialized into the fresh `server-config`
# volume — that was the build-146 bug where `/setup` rejected the documented
# default `Admin@123` (the server saw a pre-existing setup-auth.json and skipped
# seeding the default). The server recreates both on first boot.
**/db-config.json
**/setup-auth.json
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
FEATURES.md
GUIDE.md
TUTORIAL.md
SQL_SCRIPT.txt
.github/
.storybook/
.stories/
*.stories.*
.mise.toml
